 fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Tennessee remains one of the most reliably Republican states in presidential voting, with a partisan lean of roughly fourteen points toward the GOP and no Democratic presidential win in decades. The 2028 race is open with the incumbent term-limited, so no incumbency advantage applies to either side. No polls of the state's presidential contest are available yet, and no expert ratings have been published.\n\nThe forecast therefore rests on fundamentals, which point to a Republican win in the mid-teens. Headlines from Tennessee's 2026 Senate and governor races show continued Republican strength downballot, though one report noted Trump's approval underwater, a national signal that could matter if it deepens. Prediction markets and pollsters have not yet focused on this contest. Expect a Republican margin near fourteen points, with only modest chances of a Democratic upset.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0961, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1038, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1086, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0965, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1008, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1057, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -14.0}]}